ord-257bm-i11c"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-i11c"],"id":"long.record-257bm-i11c","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 6.102 (Uniqueness of the finite greedy representation)","locator":"Long record Proposition 6.102, p. 73, label record:257bm-i11c","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $1\\le M$, $0\\le R\\le M$, and $0\\le a<2^{M-R}$. If\n$$\n\\sum_{d=2}^{R}\\varepsilon_d\n       \\left\\lfloor\\frac{2^M}{2^d-1}\\right\\rfloor+a\n       =2^{M-1}-1,\\qquad \\varepsilon_d\\in\\{0,1\\},\n$$\nthen $\\varepsilon$ is the greedy word for capacity $2^{M-1}-1$ and $a$ is its remainder. This follows by applying Theorem 6.100 with the preceding gap inequality. The statement identifies any such representation; it does not prove that a representation with $a<2^{M-R}$ exists. The degenerate formal case $M=0$ has empty word and zero target, using truncated natural-number subtraction.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-i11c","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-i11c","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i11c%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.BooleanMobiusGreedyReduction.localMersenneHalfTarget_lower_word_eq_greedy_and_remainder_eq%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i11c%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.BooleanMobiusGreedyReduction.localMersenneHalfTarget_lower_word_eq_greedy_and_remainder_eq%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.BooleanMobiusGreedyReduction.localMersenneHalfTarget_lower_word_eq_greedy_and_remainder_eq"},{"deriv